# Learning Records

When touching problem exposure logs, solving attempts, test/exam sessions,
solve-time measurement, reliability scoring, or the recommendation engine,
**read `docs/architecture/learning-records.md` first.** It records decisions made
on 2026-07-25 that are not obvious from the schema alone.

Current state: schema, write RPCs, and analytics views exist on the server.
**Nothing writes to them yet — the iPad student app is the trigger.**

## Non-negotiables

1. Event tables are append-only. A retry is a new `learning_attempts` row with a
   higher `attempt_no`, never an UPDATE of the previous result.
2. Never let the client compute `attempt_no`, `exposure_seq`, or
   `reliability_score`. Server triggers own those columns.
3. Never collapse the reliability axes (`supervision`, `answer_access`,
   `scored_by`, `timing_source`, `platform`, `location_kind`, `material_kind`,
   `time_limit`) into a single enum. They move independently.
4. Never hardcode a reliability score. Change
   `learning_reliability_weights` + version, then call
   `learning_reliability_recompute()`.
5. Log every problem that was shown via `learning_log_exposures`, even if it was
   never attempted. Otherwise "shown vs attempted" is unrecoverable.
6. Keep `duration_source` honest: `measured` only for real per-item timing,
   `derived_from_range` for range-split estimates.
7. Never treat `FREEPLAY` (self-paced) data as ability evidence — self-selection
   bias. Volume metrics only.

## Before adding a new test type

Check whether the `blueprint` ratios of an existing template (especially
`DAILY30`: new / retention / prerequisite / anchor) can absorb it. Student load
is already high; prefer composition changes over new sessions.

For broad changes in this area, offer the user 2-3 concrete options first.
